.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt PKCS12_ADD_SAFE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PKCS12_add_safe ,
.Nm PKCS12_add_safe_ex ,
.Nm PKCS12_add_safes ,
.Nm PKCS12_add_safes_ex
.Nd Create and add objects to a PKCS#12 structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/pkcs12.h
.Ft int
.Fo PKCS12_add_safe
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS7) **psafes"
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS12_SAFEBAG) *bags"
.Fa "int safe_nid"
.Fa "int iter"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo PKCS12_add_safe_ex
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS7) **psafes"
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS12_SAFEBAG) *bags"
.Fa "int safe_nid"
.Fa "int iter"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft PKCS12 *
.Fo PKCS12_add_safes
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS7) *safes"
.Fa "int p7_nid"
.Fc
.Ft PKCS12 *
.Fo PKCS12_add_safes_ex
.Fa "STACK_OF(PKCS7) *safes"
.Fa "int p7_nid"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn PKCS12_add_safe
creates a new PKCS7 contentInfo containing the supplied
.Sy PKCS12_SAFEBAG Ns s
and adds this to a set of PKCS7 contentInfos.
Its type depends on the value of
.Fa safe_nid :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It * \&If Fa safe_nid No is -1, a plain PKCS7 Em data No contentInfo is created.
.It * \&If Fa safe_nid No is a valid PBE algorithm NID, a PKCS7 Sy encryptedData No contentInfo is created. The algorithm uses Fa pass No as the passphrase and Fa iter No as the iteration count. \&If Fa iter No is zero then a default value for iteration count of 2048 is used.
.It * \&If Fa safe_nid No is 0, a PKCS7 Sy encryptedData No contentInfo is created using a default encryption algorithm, currently Sy NID_pbe_WithSHA1And3_Key_TripleDES_CBC .
.El
.Fn PKCS12_add_safe_ex
is identical to
.Fn PKCS12_add_safe
but allows for a library context
.Fa ctx
and property query
.Fa propq
to be used to select algorithm implementations.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_add_safes
creates a
.Vt PKCS12
structure containing the supplied set of PKCS7 contentInfos.
The
.Fa safes
are enclosed first within a PKCS7 contentInfo of type
.Fa p7_nid .
Currently the only supported type is
.Sy NID_pkcs7_data .
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_add_safes_ex
is identical to
.Fn PKCS12_add_safes
but allows for a library context
.Fa ctx
and property query
.Fa propq
to be used to select algorithm implementations.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn PKCS12_add_safe
makes assumptions regarding the encoding of the given pass phrase.
See
.Xr passphrase-encoding 7
for more information.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn PKCS12_add_safe
returns a value of 1 indicating success or 0 for failure.
.Pp
.Fn PKCS12_add_safes
returns a valid
.Vt PKCS12
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Sh CONFORMING TO
IETF RFC 7292
.Pf ( Lk https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7292 )
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr PKCS12_create 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn PKCS12_add_safe_ex
and
.Fn PKCS12_add_safes_ex
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
